\begin{fdu:abstract-en}

With the rapid development of artificial intelligence, deep learning has achieved
significant breakthroughs in the field of natural language processing (NLP).
This dissertation systematically investigates key technologies of NLP based on
deep learning, focusing on three main aspects: pre-trained language models,
text generation, and knowledge graph construction.

Regarding pre-trained language models, this dissertation proposes a novel pre-training
strategy that incorporates multi-granularity semantic information, effectively enhancing
the model's ability to understand Chinese text. Experimental results demonstrate that
the proposed method achieves superior performance compared to baseline models on
multiple Chinese natural language understanding benchmarks.

In the area of text generation, this dissertation designs a knowledge-enhanced text
generation framework. By dynamically incorporating external knowledge during the
decoding phase, this framework addresses the factual error issues caused by insufficient
knowledge in traditional generation models. Experiments on multiple text generation tasks
validate the effectiveness of the proposed framework.

For knowledge graph construction, this dissertation proposes a contrastive learning-based
entity relation extraction method. By constructing positive and negative sample pairs
for contrastive training, this method significantly improves relation extraction
performance in low-resource scenarios.

The research contributions of this dissertation hold both theoretical significance and
practical value for advancing the application of deep learning in natural language
processing.

\end{fdu:abstract-en}

\end{document}
